# Apple Pay domain verification. Apple's checker (and Paystack's own docs)
# require this to be served as application/text specifically — a file with
# no extension would otherwise fall back to Cloudflare's default sniffing
# (application/octet-stream, or a download prompt in a browser), which
# fails verification and can also break live payments later. Explicit here
# rather than relying on any inferred default.
/.well-known/apple-developer-merchantid-domain-association
  Content-Type: application/text
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600

/*.html
  Cache-Control: no-cache, no-store, must-revalidate

/
  Cache-Control: no-cache, no-store, must-revalidate

# The hero photo used to live at this one fixed filename, and even with
# no-store here, Cloudflare's own edge cache (which caches image
# extensions by default regardless of origin Cache-Control) kept serving
# old bytes from some edge locations after a swap. Fixed at the root:
# each hero swap now ships as a NEW filename (images/hero-team-YYYYMMDD.jpg)
# referenced from index.html, so a stale edge-cached copy of the old
# filename is simply never requested again. No header override needed —
# just give the next swap a new filename rather than overwriting this one.
